{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L88"},"roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"title":"init(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0VyACxc14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphRzlufc"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hypergraph","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hypergraph.vertexIndexBound"},{"text":" is not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The oriented matrix of a directed hypergraph: rows by vertex index, a column per hyperedge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-6qyfl":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented matrix of a directed hypergraph: rows by vertex index, a column per hyperedge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"init(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"DirectedHypergraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":" allows both)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}}}